@page "/privacy"
@layout BlankLayout
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.AuthPages

@*
    ── מדיניות פרטיות — the one PUBLIC content page ─────────────────────────
    Required by Google for an OAuth production consent screen, so it has to
    render for a completely signed-out visitor.

    HOW IT IS PUBLIC, and why nothing else had to change: this project enforces
    authorization per PAGE, through the [Authorize] attribute that
    AuthorizeRouteView in App.razor honours. There is no fallback policy —
    Program.cs's AddAuthorizationCore only registers the named "VerifiedUser"
    policy — so a page that carries NO attribute is anonymous by construction.
    That is exactly how /Login, /Signup and /Forget-Password already work, and
    this page follows them: same folder, same BlankLayout, no attribute added
    and none removed anywhere else.

    LAYOUT: BlankLayout renders @Body with no app shell, so there is no sidebar,
    no top bar and nothing that would try to resolve a user. The design system
    is opted into explicitly by putting `motiva motiva-final` on the page root —
    the same pair AppLayout puts on the authenticated shell — so the tokens,
    the Heebo scale and the palette are the product's, not a second style.

    RTL comes from `html, body { direction: rtl }` in app.css and needs nothing
    here. Every asset path is base-relative for the sub-path deployment.
*@

